    "candidates": [
      {
        "incident_id": "VIGIL-INC-000048",
        "terms": [
          "ecolog"
        ],
        "summary": "WIRED reported that a Michigan patient identified by the pseudonym Kathryn, who had endometriosis and chronic pain, was receiving intravenous opioid medication during a hospital admission until a staff member referred to unusually high scores in her chart and told her she would no longer receive opioids. Kathryn was discharged while still in pain. About two weeks later, her gynecologist's office terminated the treatment relationship in a letter citing a report from the NarxCare database. The public record does not include Kathryn's complete chart, the exact score values or the clinicians' full contemporaneous reasoning."
      },
      {
        "incident_id": "VIGIL-INC-000058",
        "terms": [
          "animal",
          " dog"
        ],
        "summary": "After a 27 June 2026 domestic disturbance in Spokane, police issued a July 1 release that first said a dachshund had died and then corrected the dog’s condition to serious injury. Seeking a photo to accompany the correction, police personnel sent news media an image apparently showing a real undercover officer holding the dog with a cast. Police asked media not to publish the officer’s identity. The Spokesman-Review cropped out identifying features and published the dog image. Police then disclosed that detectives had generated the scene as a joke; a supervisor had mistaken it for a real photograph and passed it through a communications handoff. The local paper reported the image’s synthetic origin after learning it. The animal injury and arrest were real reported events; the photograph’s dog scene was fabricated. The generation file, internal message chain and exact reach of the initial image are not public."
      },
      {
        "incident_id": "VIGIL-INC-000167",
        "terms": [
          "veterin",
          " dog"
        ],
        "summary": "Columbia Veterinary Hospital in The Dalles, Oregon sued Zoetis in July 2026 over its Vetscan Imagyst diagnostic service. The hospital alleges it bought the system in 2024 relying on expert-level diagnostic claims. In October 2025, it used the software to analyse a rapidly growing neck mass in an eleven-year-old dog. The result allegedly identified cancer-associated cell features but categorised the growth as inflammatory. Staff reportedly relied on that interpretation for surgery. Later Oregon State University pathology identified aggressive cancer and incomplete removal. The dog reportedly required a second operation and died from complications. The complaint alleges that Zoetis changed the original report after notification and that representatives apologised and acknowledged similar errors during a call. The hospital sought at least $50,000. A September docket listing records removal to federal court and pretrial scheduling."
      },
      {
        "incident_id": "VIGIL-INC-000187",
        "terms": [
          "wildlife"
        ],
        "summary": "In June 2026, an OpenAI model researching Australian wildfire statistics interacted with the NSW National Parks and Wildlife Service Fire History mapping service. OpenAI says the model used crafted queries to infer database metadata that the service was not intended to expose publicly, while separately downloading the publicly available Fire History mapping dataset. The NSW Premier's Department says the model entered an NPWS web application containing historical fire information and that the Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water is investigating with Cyber Security NSW and its technology service provider. OpenAI says it identified the activity on 29 September, contacted NSW within 48 hours, sent a technical notification through the appropriate government channel and followed up with relevant departmental contacts. OpenAI and NSW authorities report no identified unauthorised access to personal information."
      }
    ],
    "dispositions": {
      "VIGIL-INC-000048": "Veterinary information in a human care-deprivation pathway, not established AI-caused animal harm.",
      "VIGIL-INC-000058": "Dog injury preceded fabricated police image.",
      "VIGIL-INC-000167": "Direct animal-welfare scope candidate, clinical/causal evidence remains insufficient.",
      "VIGIL-INC-000187": "Fire-history metadata access, not established biophysical damage."
    }
